<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: right"><B>Exhibit 99.1&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>Zhengye Biotechnology Holding Limited Regains
Compliance with Nasdaq Bid Price Requirement</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Jilin, China, August 6, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE)
-- Zhengye Biotechnology Holding Limited (Nasdaq: ZYBT) (the &ldquo;Company&rdquo; or &ldquo;Zhengye&rdquo;), a veterinary vaccine manufacturer
that encompasses research, development, manufacturing, and sales of veterinary vaccines, with a focus on livestock vaccines in China,
today announced that on August 5, 2026, the Company received a letter (the &ldquo;Compliance Letter&rdquo;) from The Nasdaq Stock Market
LLC (&ldquo;Nasdaq&rdquo;) informing the Company that it has regained compliance with the minimum bid price requirement of $1.00 per share
under Nasdaq Listing Rule 5550(a)(2).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">As previously disclosed, on May 29, 2026, the
Company received a notification letter from Nasdaq indicating that the closing bid price of the Company&rsquo;s Class A ordinary shares
had been below $1.00 per share for 30 consecutive business days. Nasdaq has since determined that, for the last 10 consecutive business
days, from July 20, 2026 to August 4, 2026, the closing bid price of the Company&rsquo;s Class A ordinary shares has been at $1.00 per
share or greater. Accordingly, the Company has regained compliance with Nasdaq Listing Rule 5550(a)(2).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Zhengye continues to be listed on The Nasdaq Capital
Market under the ticker symbol &ldquo;ZYBT&rdquo;.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>About Zhengye Biotechnology Holding Limited</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Through Jilin Zhengye Biological Products Co.,
Ltd., the Company&rsquo;s operating entity based in Jilin, China, Zhengye Biotechnology Holding Limited focuses on the research, development,
manufacturing, and sales of veterinary vaccines, with an emphasis on vaccines for livestock. For over 20 years, the operating entity has
been committed to enhancing the health of animals. The operating entity has 50 veterinary vaccines, including vaccines for swine, cattle,
goats, sheep, poultry, and dogs. The operating entity&rsquo;s products are available in 29 provincial regions across China and are exported
overseas to Vietnam, Pakistan, and Egypt as of the date of this press release. The operating entity has three veterinary vaccine production
floors (including 13 vaccine production lines), one quality examination center, and one animal facility for vaccine development, all operating
in accordance with Good Manufacturing Practices for Veterinary Drugs issued by the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs of the PRC.
For more information, please visit the Company&rsquo;s website:&nbsp;http://ir.jlzybio.com.</P>

